From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] input: process the start time seek before demuxing pictures

The input queued its start-time seek but demuxed once before processing
it. A software-decoded ASF picture could reach the surface before the
seek flush, so capturing the first output returned frame zero. Drain the
initial controls before the first demux when a start time is requested.
Only demuxers that already report a length and have a selected audio or
video stream are ready for this. MPEG-PS discovers its timeline during
the first demux; Ogg creates its streams there, even with a known length.
Both retain that initial probe rather than losing an unready seek.
The zero control deadline avoids waiting for a clock before demux starts.

---

diff --git a/src/input/input.c b/src/input/input.c
--- a/src/input/input.c
+++ b/src/input/input.c
@@ -704,6 +704,15 @@

     demux_t *p_demux = input_priv(p_input)->master->p_demux;
     const bool b_can_demux = p_demux->pf_demux != NULL;
+    /* Some demuxers discover their timeline (MPEG-PS) or create their streams
+     * (Ogg) only on the first demux. An early seek needs both a known length
+     * and a selected stream; otherwise retain that initial probe. */
+    vlc_tick_t i_length;
+    bool b_initial_seek = input_priv(p_input)->i_start > 0 &&
+                          (var_GetInteger( p_input, "video-es" ) >= 0 ||
+                           var_GetInteger( p_input, "audio-es" ) >= 0) &&
+                          !demux_Control( p_demux, DEMUX_GET_LENGTH, &i_length ) &&
+                          i_length > 0;

     while( !input_Stopped( p_input ) && input_priv(p_input)->i_state != ERROR_S )
     {
@@ -716,7 +725,16 @@
             b_paused = !es_out_GetBuffering( input_priv(p_input)->p_es_out )
                     || input_priv(p_input)->master->b_eof;

-        if( !b_paused )
+        /* StartTitle queued the initial seek. Drain those controls before
+         * demuxing: a fast software decoder can otherwise display the start
+         * of the file before the seek flushes it. A zero deadline drains only
+         * the queued controls, then permits the first demux iteration. */
+        if( b_initial_seek )
+        {
+            b_initial_seek = false;
+            i_wakeup = 0;
+        }
+        else if( !b_paused )
         {
             if( !input_priv(p_input)->master->b_eof )
             {
